{"pageProps":{"eyebrow":"eunomia-bpf","page":{"layout":"document","title":"build from source","description":"If you want to run the cli, in most cases, you don't need to build your own.","descriptionIsExcerpt":true,"bodyHtml":"<p>If you want to run the cli, in most cases, you don't need to build your own.</p>\n<h2 id=\"install-dependencies\">Install Dependencies</h2>\n<p>You will need <code>clang</code>, <code>libelf</code> and <code>zlib</code> to build the examples, package names may vary across distros.</p>\n<p>On Ubuntu/Debian, you need:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">apt</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> install</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> clang</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> libelf1</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> libelf-dev</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> zlib1g-dev</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>On CentOS/Fedora, you need:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">dnf</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> install</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> clang</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> elfutils-libelf</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> elfutils-libelf-devel</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> zlib-devel</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>install rust toolchain</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">curl</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> https://sh.rustup.rs</span><span style=\"color:#6CB6FF\"> -sSf</span><span style=\"color:#F47067\"> |</span><span style=\"color:#F69D50\"> sh</span><span style=\"color:#6CB6FF\"> -s</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<h2 id=\"build-bpf-loader-rs\">build bpf-loader-rs</h2>\n<p>bpf-loader is our core library, written in Rust. It has no other dependencies except <code>libelf</code> and <code>zlib</code>.</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">make</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> bpf-loader-rs</span><span style=\"color:#768390\"> # build bpf-loader-rs</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>Note that this target runs the crate's <code>install-deps</code> step, which calls <code>apt-get</code> through <code>sudo</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"build-ecli\">build ecli</h2>\n<p>The cli tool is written in Rust as well. It links against <code>bpf-loader-rs</code> through a path dependency, so this builds both. It additionally needs OpenSSL and <code>pkg-config</code> (its own <code>install-deps</code> installs <code>libssl-dev</code> and <code>pkg-config</code> through <code>apt</code>):</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">make</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> ecli</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>The resulting binary is <code>ecli/target/release/ecli-rs</code>. <code>make release</code> at the project root packages it under the name <code>ecli</code>, together with <code>ecc</code>, into <code>eunomia.tar.gz</code>:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">make</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> release</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<h2 id=\"build-compiler\">build compiler</h2>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">make</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> ecc</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>ecc</code> fetches and builds <code>bpftool</code> and a <code>vmlinux.h</code> set of its own at build time, so it needs network access and <code>libclang</code> (for <code>bindgen</code>):</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">apt</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> install</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> libclang-dev</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>In a network-isolated environment, set <code>SANDBOX</code> to a non-empty value to skip the fetching; the build then uses the <code>BPFTOOL_DIR</code> and <code>VMLINUX_DIR</code> directories you point it at.</p>\n<p>The <code>bpftool</code> binary that <code>ecc</code> builds its workspace from comes from the <code>third_party/bpftool</code> submodule, and the <code>vmlinux.h</code> headers the compiler includes come from <code>third_party/vmlinux</code>, so a fresh clone needs them populated first:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">git</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> submodule</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> update</span><span style=\"color:#6CB6FF\"> --init</span><span style=\"color:#6CB6FF\"> --recursive</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>The resulting binary is <code>compiler/cmd/target/release/ecc-rs</code>; <code>make release</code> packages a copy of it as <code>ecc-rs</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"build-wasm-programs\">build wasm programs</h2>\n<p><code>ecc</code> can compile C to wasm. That needs WASI SDK: download a <a href=\"https://github.com/CraneStation/wasi-sdk/releases\">wasi-sdk</a> release and extract it to <code>/opt/wasi-sdk</code>. The <code>wasm-runtime</code> submodule was removed from the project, so there is no separate <code>make</code> target for it any more.</p>\n<h1 id=\"install-from-package-manager\">install from package manager</h1>\n<h2 id=\"nix\">nix</h2>\n<p>On any distros with nix installed:</p>\n<h3 id=\"build-ecc\">build ecc</h3>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">nix</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> build</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> github:eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf#ecc</span><span style=\"color:#768390\"> # or ecli, see `nix flake show` for details # or ecli</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>Run application directly with:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">nix</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> run</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> github:eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf#ecc</span><span style=\"color:#6CB6FF\"> --</span><span style=\"color:#6CB6FF\"> -h</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<h2 id=\"openeuler\">openEuler</h2>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#F69D50\">sudo</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> dnf</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> search</span><span style=\"color:#96D0FF\"> eunomia-bpf</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"color:#768390\"># and install</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<h2 id=\"more-details\">more details</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The top-level <a href=\"https://github.com/eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf/blob/master/Makefile\">Makefile</a> shows what each target delegates to; the per-component ones (<a href=\"https://github.com/eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf/blob/master/compiler/Makefile\"><code>compiler/Makefile</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf/blob/master/ecli/Makefile\"><code>ecli/Makefile</code></a>) have the details.</li>\n<li>You may want to refer to our CI for more build info: <a href=\"https://github.com/eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf/blob/master/.github/workflows/ecc-binary.yml\">ecc-binary.yml</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf/blob/master/.github/workflows/ecli-binary.yaml\">ecli-binary.yaml</a>.</li>\n</ul>","tags":[],"headings":[{"id":"install-dependencies","text":"Install Dependencies","depth":2},{"id":"build-bpf-loader-rs","text":"build bpf-loader-rs","depth":2},{"id":"build-ecli","text":"build ecli","depth":2},{"id":"build-compiler","text":"build compiler","depth":2},{"id":"build-wasm-programs","text":"build wasm programs","depth":2},{"id":"nix","text":"nix","depth":2},{"id":"build-ecc","text":"build ecc","depth":3},{"id":"openeuler","text":"openEuler","depth":2},{"id":"more-details","text":"more details","depth":2}],"sourcePath":"https://github.com/eunomia-bpf/eunomia.dev/tree/main/docs/eunomia-bpf/setup/build.en.md","metadata":{"updatedAt":"2026-11-25T15:30:03.000Z","createdAt":"2025-02-10T22:38:08.000Z","authors":[{"name":"Yunwei 123","email":"yunwei356@gmail.com"},{"name":"ϻisռad Ϙasiϻ","email":"misnadqasim@gmail.com"},{"name":"weekendfish","email":"yusen356@gmail.com"}]},"path":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/setup/build/","alternates":{"en":"/eunomia-bpf/setup/build/","zh":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/setup/build/"},"continuation":{"index":{"title":"eunomia-bpf：简化并增强eBPF，支持CO-RE[^1]和WebAssembly[^2]","description":"![GitHub release (latest by date)](https://github.com/eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf/releases) ![codecov](https://codecov.io/gh/eunomia-bpf/eunomia-bpf)","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/"},"previous":{"title":"build on android aarch64","description":"Android上build需要先Installing Debian on Android in Termux","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/setup/build-android-arm/"},"next":{"title":"Install ecli and ecc","description":"- Install the ecli tool for running eBPF program from the cloud:","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/setup/"}},"sidebar":[{"title":"eunomia-bpf：简化并增强eBPF，支持CO-RE[^1]和WebAssembly[^2]","items":[{"title":"eunomia-bpf：简化并增强eBPF，支持CO-RE[^1]和WebAssembly[^2]","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/","depth":0},{"title":"Project architecture","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/architecture/","depth":1},{"title":"benchmark","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/benchmark/","depth":1},{"title":"ecc docker usage","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/ecc/docker-usage/","depth":2},{"title":"github template","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/ecc/github-template/","depth":2},{"title":"eunomia-cc","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/ecc/","depth":1},{"title":"ecc usage","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/ecc/usage/","depth":2},{"title":"ecli dockerfile usage","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/ecli/ecli-dockerfile-usage/","depth":2},{"title":"ecli","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/ecli/","depth":1},{"title":"ecli server","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/ecli/server/","depth":2},{"title":"exporter","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/exporter/","depth":1},{"title":"usage","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/exporter/usage/","depth":2},{"title":"introduction","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/introduction/","depth":1},{"title":"eunomia-bpf 用户手册: 让 eBPF 程序的开发和部署尽可能简单","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/manual/","depth":1},{"title":"在线体验网站","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/online/","depth":1},{"title":"quickstart","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/quickstart/","depth":1},{"title":"build on android aarch64","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/setup/build-android-arm/","depth":2},{"title":"build from source","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/setup/build/","depth":2},{"title":"Install ecli and ecc","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/setup/","depth":1},{"title":"supporting-external-BTF","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/supporting-external-BTF/","depth":1},{"title":"video","href":"/zh/eunomia-bpf/video/","depth":1}]}]}},"__N_SSG":true}